13) Write a Python program to check the validity of passwords input by users.
Validation :
At least 1 letter between [a-z] and 1 letter between [A-Z].
At least 1 number between [0-9].
At least 1 character from [$#@].
Minimum length 6 characters.
Maximum length 16 characters.

password = input("Enter your password: ")

while True:
    if len(password) < 6 or len(password) > 16:
        print("Invalid password length must be 6–16)")
        break
    if not any(c.isdigit() for c in password):
        print("there is no digit in password")
        break
    if not any(c.islower() for c in password):
        print("there is no lower case letter in the password")
        break
    if not any(c.isupper() for c in password):
        print("there is no upper case letter in password")
        break
    if not any(c in "$#@" for c in password):
        print("there are no special characters in password")
        break
    print("password accepted")
    break

